	"note": "Every value is a ceiling, and a row with no budget fails rather than passing. A Chromium ceiling is the worst of two 60 second runs of the whole matrix times 1.5, except the counters the playout engine has to keep at zero (underrun episodes, skip-aheads, budget aborts), which are a hard 0 wherever both runs measured zero and a measured ceiling where they did not. A row whose two runs agreed within that 1.5 on every graded metric is enforced; the rest keep the `recorded` marker, which prints a breach and calls it out without failing the run, until the nightly runner records its own. A replay ceiling is exactly what was measured and is always enforced, because nothing in that lane can be unlucky.",
